@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-10-15
@allow-many-consumes: "Onboarding orchestrator: sequences key discovery, bootstrap, share store, and config write, each owned elsewhere."

Feature: Machine Onboarding
  "mason setup <server>: make this machine able to publish to a server in one idempotent run — find or create a key, bootstrap the server as an admin only when needed, optionally provision the share store, verify, and record the server in ~/.mason."

  Provides:
    - setup.Run @source("symbol:Run")
    - setup.Params @source("symbol:Params")
    - setup.Deps @source("symbol:Deps")
    - setup.Result @source("symbol:Result")
    - setup.Keygen @source("symbol:Keygen")
    - setup.NewSystemKeygen @source("symbol:NewSystemKeygen")
    - setup.DefaultKeyPath @source("symbol:DefaultKeyPath")

  Consumes:
    - config.ParseServer
    - config.NewShare
    - remote.SSHOptions
    - setup.BootstrapScript
    - setup.ShareStoreScript
    - setup.WriteUserConfig

  Invariants:
    - Run MUST be idempotent: on an already-working machine it changes nothing remote and only rewrites ~/.mason if a value differs
    - Run MUST try the existing SSH setup (an explicit --key, else the key ~/.mason records for this server, else agent and ~/.ssh/config) before generating a key, and MUST generate only ~/.ssh/mason (ed25519, comment mason@<hostname>) when nothing works
    - The first connection MUST trust a new host key (accept-new) and only then; every later connection uses strict checking
    - Bootstrap MUST run only when the mason user cannot be reached (or Bootstrap is forced), MUST connect as the admin user, and MUST be confirmed unless Yes
    - When the admin connection fails, Run MUST fail with the exact 'mason key add' line to run from an already-authorized machine
    - PrintOnly MUST render the scripts Run would apply and MUST change nothing, locally or remotely
    - After any remote change Run MUST verify by connecting as the mason user before writing config
    - ~/.mason MUST be written only after verification, merged with existing content; a v1 file MUST be backed up, not silently overwritten
    - Share store provisioning MUST happen only when a share URL is given, as the admin, and be confirmed unless Yes

  OutOfScope:
    - Site provisioning (provision)
    - Managing additional machines' keys (setup.KeyAdd and friends)
    - Writing ~/.ssh/config or known_hosts directly (OpenSSH owns them)

  Scenario (happy-path): Already working
    Given mason@host is reachable with the agent's key
    When Run executes
    Then no key is generated, no bootstrap runs, and ~/.mason records server

  Scenario (happy-path): Fresh server
    Given no mason user on the server and root access from this machine
    When Run executes and the bootstrap is confirmed
    Then ~/.ssh/mason is generated, the bootstrap runs as root, mason@host verifies, and ~/.mason records server and key

  Scenario (negative): No admin access
    Given mason@host is unreachable and root@host is refused
    When Run executes
    Then it fails with a 'mason key add' line containing this machine's public key

  Scenario (negative): Bootstrap declined
    Given the confirmation is answered no
    When Run executes
    Then nothing remote changes and no config is written

  Scenario (edge): Print only
    Given PrintOnly
    When Run executes
    Then Result.Scripts holds the bootstrap (and share store) scripts and nothing is changed
